  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 3.5. A layered ArchiMate view for a Quality and Continuity of Care sub-goal: 'Comprehensive Needs Assessment' and the outcome 'Integrated, Person-Centered Care' at the top; five capabilities (Care Protocol Management, Patient History Integration, Decision Support, Task-Sharing Orchestration, Quality and Performance Monitoring) realised through an 'Integrated Shared Care Plan (SCP)' product; application services for care protocols, clinical decision support, patient-history aggregation and care coordination; components such as a knowledge base engine, EMR, interoperability layer, access control, lifelong health record and client registry; and a grouping of the shared registries and terminology server they use.",
